# Load balancing core: Walking skeleton

**Part of epic** #70 · **Slice** 1 of 3 · **Depends on** none

## Goal
Two EVSEs share a site limit.

## Spec (rev 1)

### Scenarios
- **S1** — Two EVSEs share a limit
  - Given a 32 A site limit and two charging EVSEs
  - When both request 32 A
  - Then each is offered 16 A

### Requirements
| ID | Kind | Requirement |
|---|---|---|
| R1 | new | The allocator never offers more than the site limit in total. |

### Other spec changes
| File | Section | Change |
|---|---|---|
| ocpp/api-contract.md | Config keys | `site_limit_a` row (R1) |
| ocpp/api-contract.md | Notes | units are amperes throughout |

## Architecture
Adds: `Device`, `Allocator`, `Node` with minimal bodies

The skeleton every slice builds on is in epic #70, `## Architecture`.
